        "id": "def-causal-classification-of-lorentz-vectors",
        "kind": "definition",
        "domain": "mathematics",
        "title": "Timelike, null, spacelike and causal vectors of a Lorentz vector space",
        "statement": "Let (V,eta) be a Lorentz vector space. A vector v in V is timelike if eta(v,v) < 0, null (or lightlike) if v is nonzero and eta(v,v) = 0, spacelike if eta(v,v) > 0, and causal if it is timelike or null. The zero vector is none of timelike, null or spacelike. The sign of eta(v,v) is the causal character of v. The pairing eta itself is written <v,w> := eta(v,w) when no confusion arises. Each nonzero vector has exactly one causal character.",
        "strategy": "The classification is by the sign of the real number eta(v,v); the three alternatives eta(v,v) < 0, eta(v,v) = 0, eta(v,v) > 0 for v nonzero are mutually exclusive and exhaustive by trichotomy of the order on R, and the zero vector is excluded from the null case by definition.",
