        "statement": "In every oriented time-oriented affine Minkowski space (A,V,eta,C^+) and for every event o in A there exists an inertial frame with origin o; consequently inertial charts are defined at every event. Explicitly: start from any eta-orthonormal ordered basis (f_0,f_1,f_2,f_3) of V; if f_0 is not in C^+ then replacing f_0 by -f_0 makes the first vector future (because the timelike set is the disjoint union of C^+ and C^- and eta(-f_0,-f_0) = eta(f_0,f_0)); the resulting ordered basis has some orientation class, and if that class is negative (det M = -1 relative to the fixed orientation) then replacing e_1 by -e_1 (or interchanging e_1 and e_2) produces a positively oriented ordered basis, without destroying eta-orthonormality and without changing the first, future vector.",
