        "title": "The affine atlas makes the Minkowski model a smooth 4-manifold diffeomorphic to R^4",
        "statement": "Let (A,V,eta,C^+) be an oriented time-oriented affine Minkowski space and let x: A -> R^4 be one inertial chart. Give A the topology in which a set U is open exactly when x(U) is open in R^4 (the transported topology; it is the unique topology making x a homeomorphism onto R^4). Then: (i) A is a Hausdorff, second-countable topological 4-manifold; (ii) the one-chart family {x} is a smooth atlas, so A is a smooth 4-manifold and x is a diffeomorphism onto R^4 with its standard smooth structure; (iii) every affine chart of A, i.e. every map of the form y(p) = M x(p) + b with M an invertible 4x4 real matrix and b in R^4, and in particular every inertial chart, belongs to the same smooth structure, and its transition with x is the smooth diffeomorphism u |-> M u + b of R^4 with inverse u |-> M^{-1}(u-b); (iv) the topology and smooth structure do not depend on the choice of the initial inertial chart x.",
        "strategy": "For (i): x is by construction a homeomorphism A -> R^4; R^4 is Hausdorff, second-countable and locally Euclidean, and each of these properties transfers along a homeomorphism (separate points by preimages of disjoint open neighbourhoods; pull back a countable basis; use x itself as a global coordinate chart). For (ii): a one-chart family vacuously satisfies smooth compatibility, so {x} is a smooth atlas; the maximal atlas it generates is the smooth structure, and in this structure the coordinate representation of x is the identity, so x is a diffeomorphism onto R^4 equipped with the standard structure. For (iii): if y = M x + b is an affine chart, then y is a homeomorphism for the same topology and the transition y o x^{-1} is the map u |-> M u + b, whose components are polynomials of degree at most 1 in the coordinates; linear maps and constant maps of R^4 are smooth, and sums of smooth functions are smooth, so y o x^{-1} is smooth (one can differentiate componentwise using the algebra of total derivatives and the theorem that continuous partial derivatives imply total differentiability). Its inverse u |-> M^{-1}(u-b) is again affine and smooth, so y belongs to the same smooth structure; every inertial chart has this form by the transition formula of the frame definition. For (iv): if x' is another inertial chart, then x' = M x + b for an affine map of the displayed form, so the topologies transported by x and x' coincide and the two suggested one-chart atlases generate the same maximal atlas.",
