        "statement": "Let (A,V,eta,C^+) be an oriented time-oriented affine Minkowski space and let (o;e_0,...,e_3) be an inertial frame. For v_0,...,v_3 in V let [v_j^a] be the 4x4 matrix whose j-th column lists the coordinates of v_j in the ordered basis (e_0,...,e_3), and define epsilon(v_0,v_1,v_2,v_3) := det([v_j^a]) in the sense of the determinant of a square matrix. Then epsilon is an alternating 4-linear form on V, called the oriented volume form of the model. Its components in the inertial frame are the permutation symbols epsilon_{abcd}, with epsilon_{0123} = +1 and epsilon_{abcd} the sign of the permutation taking (0,1,2,3) to (a,b,c,d) (zero if two indices repeat). The raised components are epsilon^{abcd} := eta^{aa'} eta^{bb'} eta^{cc'} eta^{dd'} epsilon_{a'b'c'd'}, where eta^{ab} is the inverse of the matrix eta_{ab}; epsilon^{0123} = -1. The spatial permutation symbol epsilon_{ijk} for i,j,k in {1,2,3} is defined by epsilon_{123} = +1 together with alternation.",
